  "query_preview": "inland/south.\n\nThis fresh to strong northeast flow will produce a number of \nbeach and marine hazards, including rough surf, large breaking \nwaves, and a high risk of life-threatening rip currents at area \nbeaches. Entering the dangerous surf is highly discouraged! Long \nperiod onshore swells will also likely contribute to moderate \nbeach erosion through multiple high tide cycles this weekend into \nearly next week. A High Risk for rip currents exists for area \nbeaches the next several days, with a High Surf Advisory going \ninto effect later this evening and continues through the weekend \nas seas continue to build. \n\nMonday-Friday (Modified Previous Discussion)...A tight pressure \ngradient continues across the area into next week, as a strong \narea of high pressure remains situated over the eastern U.S., the \nstrong low meanders off the Mid-Atlantic/Northeast U.S. coast, and\nthe stationary front lingers to the south. This will maintain a \nbreezy to windy N/NE flow for much of the week, continuing rough \nsurf, large breaking waves, a high risk of life-threatening rip \ncurrents, and moderate beach erosion at area beaches, as well as \nhazardous boating conditions in the Atlantic waters through at \nleast early this coming week. Rounds of isolated to scattered \nonshore moving showers remain in the forecast, with drier \nconditions generally forecast inland. Temperatures generally \nremain below normal, with highs in the upper 70s to low 80s and \novernight lows in the 60s.",
